=== Scientific names ===
{{shortcut|MOS:ITALSCINAMES|MOS:SCIENTIFIC}}
{{Main|Wikipedia:Manual of Style/Organisms}}
<!-- Please keep these instructions consistent with both MOS:LIFE (the summary) and MOS:ORGANISMS (the page). -->
[[Scientific name]]s of organisms are formatted according to normal [[Taxonomy (biology)|taxonomic nomenclature]].
* Do not italicize (but do capitalize) taxa higher than [[genus]] (exceptions are below).
** [[Virus]] taxonomy is a partial exception; current scientific practice is to italicize all ranks of taxa (even those higher than genus; e.g., ''[[Ortervirales]]'', an order, or ''[[Herpesviridae]]'', a family).  However, this should only be done in articles about viruses or virology; mentions of virus taxa in articles about other forms of life should follow the normal rules for italicizing scientific names.
* Italicize all lower [[Rank (zoology)#All ranks|ranks (taxa)]]: [[genus]] (capitalized), [[subgenus]] (capitalized), [[species]], [[subspecies]].
** Names of genera are always italicized (and capitalized), even when not paired with a species name: {{xt|''Allosaurus'', ''Falco'', ''Anas''}}.
** The entire [[Binomial nomenclature|binomial]] or [[Trinomial nomenclature|trinomial]] scientific name is italicized, whether given in full or abbreviated: ({{xt|''Liriodendron tulipifera''}}, {{xt|''N. v. piaropicola''}}).
* Interpolations such as "cf.", "×", "var.", or "subsp." are not italicized: {{xt|''Ninox'' cf. ''novaeseelandiae''}}, {{xt|the chaussie is a hybrid cat (''Felis catus'' × ''chaus'')}}.
* Parenthetic expressions should not be italicized unless part of the scientific name, as in the case of a subgenus, which is always italicized, though the parentheses (round brackets) are not: {{xt|''Cypraea'' (''Cypraea'') ''tigris''}}.
* Do not italicize authorities (author names) juxtaposed with scientific names: {{xt|Subgenus ''Potentilla'' {{small|Syme}} and subgenus ''Hypargyrium'' {{small|(Fourr.) Juz.}} have been combined under subgenus ''Potentilla'' {{small|Syme}}}}. In the article body, wrap the authority information in {{tl|small}} or <nowiki><small>...</small></nowiki>. (This need not be done for authorities in a taxobox that are entered using parameters such {{para|authority}} or {{para|parent_authority}}, since small text is then used automatically. For synonym lists, either use templates like {{tl|Species list}} which automatically use small text for authorities, or wrap the authority information as described above.)

Derived uses in non-biological contexts are not italicized: {{xt|The largest carnivore in family Tyrannosauridae was ''[[Tyrannosaurus|T. rex]]'' itself}}, but {{xt|''Unicorn'' was an album by the band [[T. Rex (band)|T. Rex]]}}.

Although often derived from Latin or Ancient Greek, scientific names are never marked up with {{tl|lang}} or related templates.

